# How to cite innerVANI. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository".
# Format: https://citation-file-format.github.io
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use innerVANI or its standard in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "innerVANI: an open conscience layer for AI assistants"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Saha
    given-names: Avish
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1124-7119"
  - name: "The innerVANI contributors"
abstract: >-
  innerVANI is an open, model-agnostic conscience layer for AI assistants. It
  reviews what an AI is about to say or do against a public standard, the
  Conscience Foundation, and returns PASS, REVISE, ASK or DECLINE, naming the
  principles behind each verdict. It targets failures of character, such as
  flattery, invented facts, giving way under pushback, reckless actions, and
  needless refusals or lectures, and it measures over-correction as carefully
  as failure.
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - AI ethics
  - sycophancy
  - hallucination
  - over-refusal
  - LLM evaluation
  - guardrails
repository-code: "https://github.com/innervani/innervani"
url: "https://github.com/innervani/innervani"
